M2.4: choosing the cpu_hash accumulator fold

Three folds, built as three separate binaries from the same source and run ALTERNATELY
(not one after the other) so thermal drift hits all of them equally. Each measurement is
the median of 21 trials at 50 ms, 1 thread; 9 repetitions per binary.

The XOR fold was the original. It had to go: the batch is 64 Ki ops over 64 blocks, so
every block is hashed exactly 1024 times and an even number of XORs of the same value
cancels. The digest was identically 0 at the end of every batch - a sink that provably
carries nothing out of the loop, and untestable.

=== study 1: xor vs multiply-accumulate ===
rep 0 xor     median 1.334e+08 ops/s  cov 0.208
rep 0 muladd  median 1.274e+08 ops/s  cov 0.081
rep 1 xor     median 1.297e+08 ops/s  cov 0.158
rep 1 muladd  median 1.264e+08 ops/s  cov 0.228
rep 2 xor     median 1.283e+08 ops/s  cov 0.120
rep 2 muladd  median 1.249e+08 ops/s  cov 0.073
rep 3 xor     median 1.345e+08 ops/s  cov 0.101
rep 3 muladd  median 1.255e+08 ops/s  cov 0.085
rep 4 xor     median 1.295e+08 ops/s  cov 0.147
rep 4 muladd  median 1.249e+08 ops/s  cov 0.109
rep 5 xor     median 1.282e+08 ops/s  cov 0.209
rep 5 muladd  median 1.28e+08 ops/s  cov 0.099
rep 6 xor     median 1.3e+08 ops/s  cov 0.170
rep 6 muladd  median 1.209e+08 ops/s  cov 0.216
rep 7 xor     median 1.298e+08 ops/s  cov 0.071
rep 7 muladd  median 1.29e+08 ops/s  cov 0.065
rep 8 xor     median 1.329e+08 ops/s  cov 0.101
rep 8 muladd  median 1.244e+08 ops/s  cov 0.172

xor     n=9  median-of-medians 1.298e+08  min 1.282e+08  max 1.345e+08
muladd  n=9  median-of-medians 1.255e+08  min 1.209e+08  max 1.29e+08

muladd / xor = 0.9665

