xor     n=9  median-of-medians 1.36e+08  min 1.231e+08  max 1.372e+08
add     n=9  median-of-medians 1.312e+08  min 1.2e+08  max 1.393e+08
muladd  n=9  median-of-medians 1.289e+08  min 1.192e+08  max 1.342e+08

add / xor = 0.9644
muladd / xor = 0.9477

Conclusion: the non-cancelling folds cost 3-5% of the reported rate. Multiply-accumulate
was chosen anyway - it is order-dependent and cannot cancel, so the digest is a real
checksum over every block the batch touched, which CpuHash.ConsumesEveryBlockAndFoldsThemAll
checks. The run-to-run spread (+/-6%) is wider than the gap between the three folds, so
the ordering is consistent across both studies but the exact percentage is not precise.
